# What the SHELL image is: the modules it executes in place, and the
# number of kernel processes it needs.
#
# One of these files per init, and the mkfile beside them picks the one
# named after the init it is building.  Both facts in it are properties
# of the init -- which modules an image runs, and how many processes
# running them takes -- and keeping them in one place is not tidiness:
# they used to be two edits in two files with nothing connecting them,
# and a station image built with the shell image's process count comes
# up, prints its address, and then says "no procs for kproc" for ever,
# which looks like a board that booted.  flashverify.sh grew a check for
# exactly that pairing.  Now there is nothing to pair.  They are not copies of each
# other: a module is in a list because the image's init runs it, and
# which modules an init runs is the difference between the images.
#
# WHAT BEING OUTSIDE THE LIST MEANS.  The root section of the config
# still carries every module as its raw .dis, so a module left out of
# here is still in the filesystem -- but on this part it is not
# runnable.  Loading /dis/sh.dis asks malloc for 73536 bytes for its
# Inst array alone, against 147456 bytes of RAM in the whole board, and
# libinterp/load.c builds that array at load time for a module that has
# no prepared one.  So a station image carries a shell it cannot run.
# See doc/xip.ms and the XIPMODS comment in the mkfile.
#
# And the sizes are why there are two lists at all.  Decoded, measured
# from the generated prog.s: sh.dis 73332 bytes, sh/std.dis 23604,
# lil.dis 25356, sed.dis 21636, ax25chk.dis 14376, in an image that may
# not pass 913408.
#
# AND SED IS NOT IN IT ANY MORE, which is the first time this list has
# had to give something up.  The attitude and orbit simulation --
# orbitsim.c, the quaternion model in imubmx160.c, the battery curve in
# pwradm1176.c -- is about ten kilobytes of kernel text, and this image
# was already four kilobytes over the ceiling before the accuracy work
# on it; it has not been flashable since orbitsim.c landed, and nothing
# said so because the satellite image is the one being flashed.  sed is
# the largest item nothing on this board uses: no init runs it, no
# script in /lib does, and 21636 bytes is three times what was needed.
# It is still in the root as a raw module, like mount below, so it is
# there to be read and not to be run.
#
# AND IT HAS GIVEN UP A SECOND THING: ax25chk, which this file nominated
# by size when sed went.  What paid for it is the "ssl" line in the
# conf: #D costs 26480 bytes of kernel text, the styx image absorbs it
# at 629880 of 913408, and this one was already within fourteen
# kilobytes of the ceiling -- it came to 926280, which is 12872 over.
#
# The cost falls in the wrong place and it is worth saying so.  ssl is
# wanted by the SATELLITE and GROUND images, where doc/radio-plan.ms's
# steps 5 and 6 live; this is the image somebody types at.  A conf has
# one dev section for every init built from it, so there is no way to
# carry #D in one image and not another without four diverging confs.
# That is a trade recorded rather than a problem solved.
#
# ax25chk checks AX.25 framing at the bench and the station image
# (armv7max25) still carries it, which is where it is used.  Here it is
# still in the root to be read, like sed and mount; it is not runnable.
#
# The next candidate by size is dd (9852), and it has NOT been given up
# because the margin does not require it yet: this image comes to 911168
# of 913408, which is 2240 bytes spare.  That is tight enough that the
# next kernel change may break it, and the reason for leaving it there
# rather than buying headroom in advance is that the break is LOUD now
# -- the hex is its own target and bin2ihex's refusal fails the recipe,
# which it did not before five flashes wrote a stale image.
XIPDIS=\
	sh.dis\
	sh/std.dis\
	lil.dis\
	lib/arg.dis\
	lib/bufio.dis\
	lib/daytime.dis\
	lib/env.dis\
	lib/filepat.dis\
	lib/names.dis\
	lib/rand.dis\
	lib/readdir.dis\
	lib/regex.dis\
	lib/string.dis\
	lib/workdir.dis\
	echo.dis\
	radiocal.dis\
	radiocfg.dis\
	lib/radiocal.dis\
	md5sum.dis\
	strings.dis\
	ax25raw.dis\
	ax25up.dis\
	export.dis\
	cat.dis\
	dd.dis\
	ls.dis\
	bind.dis\
	pwd.dis\
	cd.dis\
	grep.dis\
	wc.dis\
	date.dis\
	sleep.dis\
	ps.dis\
	basename.dis\
	cleanname.dis\
	sort.dis\
	uniq.dis\
	tee.dis\
	tr.dis\
	test.dis\
	time.dis\
	kill.dis\
	read.dis\
	env.dis\
	xd.dis\
	seq.dis\

# Five.  A shell, its redirections and lil all work at five; at seven lil
# prints its banner and dies and even echo begins to fail, because a
# process slot is a 4096-byte kernel stack out of about 160K.  See the
# nprocwanted comment in the config.
NPROC=5

# The files this image carries that the root section does not.
#
# mount(1), so that this image can be a GROUND STATION: the satellite
# exports a namespace over the radio and the ground mounts it, which is
# what doc/pycubed-plan.ms calls the whole argument.  sys->mount is a
# system call and the shell has no builtin for it, so without this file
# there is no way to mount anything from a prompt on this board.
#
# It is here and not in the conf because the satellite image has no use
# for it -- a satellite exports, it does not mount -- and a file in the
# conf is carried by every image built from it.  That is the mechanism
# os/inferno/port/mkroot grew EXTRAROOT for, and this is the first thing
# it bought: taking the mission modules out of this image freed 6240
# bytes, which is more than mount costs.
# NOT in the XIP list above, deliberately.  Its decoded instruction
# array costs 14440 bytes of flash against 5341 for the raw module, and
# this image has about ten thousand to spare -- so mount is carried as
# a plain root file and libinterp builds its array in RAM at load time,
# like a module on any ordinary machine.  It is a short-lived command
# run by hand, not something the image runs continuously, which is
# exactly the trade XIPMODS is for and exactly when not to take it.
EXTRAROOT=\
	/dis/mount.dis			/dis32/mount.dis\

# The pool split, 50/49/1, which is what the comment in the conf records
# being measured at a shell prompt: main holds about 75K there and the
# Dis heap the rest.  image-armv7mstyx says why a satellite wants the
# opposite.
MAINPCNT=50
HEAPPCNT=49
IMAGEPCNT=1
